{
  "repo": "ARMOR-NODE-RADAR",
  "ecosystem": "armor",
  "tagline": "A radar node of up to 270 degrees: three LD2450 on three UARTs, a web panel, signed updates and a link to the broker, on one firmware for every board.",
  "description": "The firmware of ARMOR-NODE-RADAR reads up to three radars, keeps a track's identity, publishes the messages the ARMOR-COMMON contract accepts, serves a web panel with its own HTTPS certificate and installs only signed updates. It is the one node that exists as hardware; the perimeter engine, the LD2461 and presence-sensor decoders and the TLS link to the broker have not run with real modules or on a board.",
  "columns": [
    "WHAT IS CONNECTED",
    "THIS FIRMWARE",
    "WHO IT TALKS TO"
  ],
